at the back of the head, such as that worn by men in Imperial China.", "tags": ["historical"], "examples": ["A large number of loyal officials, rather than shave the front part of the head and wear the Manchu queue, voluntarily shaved the whole head, […]"], "quotes": [{"text": "[…], there were seated astraddle the whole hundred of the baronet's musqueteers, each engaged in plaiting into a queue the hair of the man who sat in front of him.", "reference": "1889, A[rthur] Conan Doyle, chapter XIX, in Micah Clarke: […], London: Longmans, Green, and Co […], →OCLC:"}, {"text": "Caparisoned for a week in purple velvet knee-length pantaloons, a red silk jacket with buckles of shiny brass, and a white goat's-hair wig which culminated behind in a saucy queue, I must have presented an exotic sight […]", "reference": "1967, William Styron, The Confessions of Nat Turner, Vintage, published 2004, page 176:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ba", "name": "Bashkir"}, "word": "толом"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "опа́шка"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "辮子 /辫子"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "hårpisk"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "letti"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "palmikko"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "natte"}, {"language": {"code": "ka", "name": "Georgian"}, "word": "ნაწნავი"}, {"language": {"code": "ka", "name": "Georgian"}, "word": "დალალი"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "αλογοουρά"}, {"language": {"code": "ja", "name": "Japanese"}, "word": "辮髪"}, {"language": {"code": "mnc", "name": "Manchu"}, "word": "ᠰᠣᠨᠴᠣᡥᠣ"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "fryzura"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "rabicho"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "rabo de cavalo"}, {"langua